.TH GETUID 2 "2026-09-06" "EpinAnonymOS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
getuid \- Linux syscall 102, as implemented by the EpinAnonymOS kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syscall(102, ...)
.br
kernel handler: \fBlinux_sys_getuid\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
--- Identity / session / group ---
Phase 10 / IR-P3: identity is read from the active task's User object. The
default subject is non-root; privileged actions are gated by typed admin
capabilities, not uid 0.
.SH IMPLEMENTATION
Dispatched from \fIsrc/kernel/d/core/kernel_main.d\fR;
implemented in \fIsrc/kernel/d/core/syscalls/posix.d\fR.
.SH CAVEAT
This kernel emulates a SUBSET of the Linux ABI.  Behaviour that stock Linux
guarantees is not guaranteed here unless the DESCRIPTION says so.  Notably,
AF_UNIX reads return EAGAIN on an empty socket rather than blocking, and
absolute opens are resolved against the calling task's namespace.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR anonymos-syscalls (7)
